1115:
(a) Definitions. For purposes of this section, the following terms shall have the meanings ascribed to them below:
Illegal street racing and reckless driving exhibitions shall mean a motor vehicle contest or event using public highways, streets, rights-of-way, public or private driveways, or public or private parking lots in violation of applicable motor vehicle and traffic laws, including without limitation O.C.G.A. §§ 40-6-186, 40-6-251, and 40-6-390. Illegal street racing or reckless driving exhibitions may include, but is not limited to situations in which:
(1) A group of individuals or motor vehicles has arrived at a location for the purpose of participating in the event;
(2) A group of individuals has gathered on private property open to the general public without consent of the owner, operator or agent of the property for the purpose of participating in the event;
(3) One or more individuals has impeded the free public use of a public street, sidewalk, or highway by actions, words or physical barriers for the purpose of conducting the event;
(4) Two or more vehicles have lined up with motors running for an illegal motor vehicle speed contest or exhibition;
(5) One or more drivers is revving his engine or spinning his tires in preparation for the event;
(6) An individual is stationed at or near one or more motor vehicles for the purpose of serving as a race or event starter.
Organizer shall mean any individual who in any manner knowingly takes part in the planning, organization, coordination, facilitation, advertising, or location sharing of illegal street racing or reckless driving exhibitions, or who collects money in connection with an illegal street race or reckless driving exhibition.
Participant shall mean any individual who is knowingly present at an illegal street race or reckless driving exhibition for the purpose of actively taking part in the event, through conduct including, but not limited to, riding as a passenger in race or exhibition vehicle, assisting organizers or drivers in carrying out or promoting the event, taking video or photographic images for purposes of promotion or profit, or exchanging money or anything of value with any driver, motor vehicle owner, organizer, or other participant in connection with the event.
(b) Violations.
(1) No person shall knowingly act as an organizer of an illegal street racing or reckless driving exhibition.
(2) Except as provided elsewhere in this section, no person shall knowingly act as a participant in, or spectator of, an illegal street racing or reckless driving exhibition.
(3) Nothing in this section prohibits law enforcement officers or their agents from being participants or spectators at an illegal street race or reckless driving exhibition in the course of their official duties.
(4) This article shall not apply to licensed or duly authorized racetracks, drag strips, or other designated areas set aside by proper authorities for such purposes.
(5) In all cases of violations of this article, the person charged shall appear in the city municipal court.
(c) Proving violations. Notwithstanding any other provision of law, to prove a violation of this article, admissible evidence may include, but is not limited to, any of the following:
(1) The time of day;
(2) The nature and description of the scene;
(3) The number of people at the scene;
(4) The location of the individual charged in relation to any individual or group present at the scene;
(5) The number and description of motor vehicles at the scene;
(6) That the individual charged drove or was transported to the scene;
(7) That the individual charged has previously participated in illegal street racing or reckless driving exhibitions;
(8) That the individual charged has previously aided and abetted illegal street racing or reckless driving exhibitions;
(9) That the individual charged has previously organized illegal street racing or reckless driving exhibitions; or
(10) That the individual charged previously was present at a location where preparations were being made for illegal street racing or reckless driving exhibitions or where illegal street racing or reckless driving exhibition was in progress.
(d) Penalties.
(1) Violations of this article shall be punished as by a fine of at least $500.00 and not more than $1,000.00, imprisonment for a term not to exceed six months, or any combination thereof, subject to all limitations contained in applicable state law.
(2) Any motor vehicle used in illegal street racing or reckless driving exhibition may be removed and impounded by a city marshal or other law enforcement officer with jurisdiction to the extent authorized by applicable state law, or pursuant to a warrant issued by a court of competent jurisdiction. An impounded vehicle may be held for not less than 30 days or final adjudication of the case, to the maximum extent allowed under state law.
(Ord. No. 2024-01-269, § 1, 2-27-2024)
